e_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Using a change point near t\u224817550 with \u00b15000 half-windows, all 12 group members switch to an essentially disjoint contact set. Pre-window partners are drawn from a stable pool {123,208,283,497,616,829,899,1064,1097,1377,1442,1519,1574,1610,1660,1931,1950} (steps 05,09,12,14,18,20,22,24,31), while post-window partners come from {160,350,462,581,861,871,945,1057,1088,1194,1277,1331,1449,1670,1863,1884,1934,1947} (steps 06,10,13,15,19,21,23,25,32). Jaccard overlap is ~0 for every member, and the switch is synchronous across the whole group rather than staggered. The transition is short: group activity drops to 1 event in [16551,17050] and 0 in [17051,18550], bracketed by 34 events in [15551,16550] and 25 in [18551,19550] (steps 28,29,30) \u2014 a clean quiescent seam. Confounders checked: total group volume is flat across the period (step 03), so this is not an activity-volume artifact; and the old partners are essentially silent after the switch while the new partners were essentially silent before it (steps 26,27), so the new links are not merely globally popular hubs, nor were the old contacts still available and gradually shed. Pre-change windows (steps 04,08) show the old pool persisting stably for ~10k units, ruling out gradual background turnover."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_c1b49572\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [214, 315, 522, 860, 919, 1085, 1390, 1431, 1589, 1672, 1860, 1936],\n  \"window\": [2551, 32551],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"