hecked: total group volume is flat across the period (step 03), so this is not an activity-volume artifact; and the old partners are essentially silent after the switch while the new partners were essentially silent before it (steps 26,27), so the new links are not merely globally popular hubs, nor were the old contacts still available and gradually shed. Pre-change windows (steps 04,08) show the old pool persisting stably for ~10k units, ruling out gradual background turnover.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 44687, "total_output_tokens": 6274, "total_tokens": 50961, "total_latency_ms": 79031, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}